                <pb facs="0704" n="632" xml:id="pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14457/7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Adee refers to legation’s telegram of August 1 relative to the inquiry of the
                    Netherlands minister for foreign affairs concerning the possibility of coercive
                    action in regard to Venezuela, and says he is directed by the Secretary of State
                    to answer that the Government of the United States should not feel at liberty to
                    object to measures of the character described in the minister’s question not
                    involving occupation of territory either permanent or of such a character as to
                    threaten permanency.</p>
            </div>
